  "pipeline": {
    "bake": "Cycles CPU at 1024 square in Blender 5.2.2. Both final triangulated receivers share UV0. Assembled AO uses twelve rays, then high/low component pairs bake separately with hard-boundary receiver fallback. A direct finish bake repairs empty rays on nonblack surfaces with that receiver’s own base color, tangent normal, ORM with contact AO, and emissive. Atlas geometry, corner normals and UV0 are hashed before and after baking.",
    "maps": "Base color and emissive use sRGB. Normal and AO/roughness/metalness use linear. KTX-Software 4.4.2 UASTC, full 11-level chains, rd orientation, packed with exact PNG fallback plus standalone maps.",
    "determinism": "Two fresh factory-startup builds and separate KTX encodes matched geometry.json, four PNGs, four KTX2s, both geometry buffers, both glTF JSONs and both GLBs byte for byte; Blender archive hashes identify the delivered editable sources.",
    "render": "Blender 5.2.2 EEVEE, 624 square, 16 samples, AgX. Floor/table/wall and heel contact are independently measured after import. Matched high and compressed-color low images share saved world camera transforms."
  },
  "corrections": [
    "The initial smart projection folded a small set of triangles. The generator moves intersecting UV triangles into dedicated space, and independent re-import verification checks the combined atlas.",
    "High-to-low rays missed the coarse scallop at some azimuths. A receiver-material fallback repaired 23,234 texels. The decoded-color regression rejected ten probes in original LOD0 and 132 probes in original LOD1. On the first repair it caught a separate 1.74-square-texel face. The final unwrap reserves new space for overlapped faces and all triangles under four square texels, with at least three texels of altitude on each relocated triangle.",
    "The imported root uses quaternion rotation. Pose checks and review scenes explicitly select Euler rotation before applying the requested wall pose, and the numerical check compares to an independently specified normal.",
    "The distance shoe omits hidden bevel strips while preserving the full contact area and center bearing interface."
  ],
